-/* A row's twig: from its trunk, a curve into an arm whose line is centred on the mark's visible centre
-   (--mark-mid), ending --tree-twig-gap before the marker. It is drawn from the marker, whose top is where the row's
-   baseline puts it (the static position of an absolute box in it), and laid out across the row (its containing block)
-   like the guides. Its upright part overlaps the trunk's end in the same colour, so the line is unbroken. */
+/* A row's twig: from its trunk, a curve into an arm that meets the mark's centre and ends --tree-twig-gap before the
+   marker. An absolute box of the marker, laid out across the row like the guides. It gets the mark's box and
+   translate, so both round to device pixels alike. */
 .conversation-row:has(> .tree-guide) > .nav-marker::before {
 	--level: var(--depth);
 	position: absolute;
 	align-self: start;
 	box-sizing: border-box;
 	inset-inline-start: calc(var(--nav-edge) + var(--from) + var(--nav-icon) / 2 - var(--tree-line) / 2);
 	inline-size: calc(var(--to) - var(--from) - var(--nav-icon) / 2 + var(--tree-line) / 2 - var(--tree-twig-gap));
